## Le post, trilingue

🇬🇧 EN / 🇯🇵 日本語 / 🇫🇷 FR

Today I focused on UV texel harmony across the whole church.

The problem I had was simple: from one pattern to the next, my UVs had no global harmony. So I took my height map, which already gave me a clear pattern, and pushed it into the base color just to get a proper debug view. Then, instead of patching things by hand with compensation sliders, I simply set one global texel density and computed the whole thing properly, so that every part of the building shares the same scale. From there, any tiling texture can go on top and the parameters stay fully editable.

Here is an extract of the UVs directly on the geometry, plus a second extract with the full materials applied. Some details can still be improved, the windows mostly, where a few UVs stay slightly stretched.

thanks for reading, like for more! ᕙ(`▿´)ᕗ

